    "measurementTechnique": [
      "Samples were collected across central Svalbard in 2021. Site metadata, including general environmental information, were manually recorded in the field. See WHONDRS_YDE21_Sampling_Protocol.pdf for details on sample and site metadata collection. Surface water samples were syringe-filtered into pre-acidified vials in the field and refrigerated until ready for laboratory processing that included solid phase extraction (SPE) before FTICR-MS analysis. Sediment samples were frozen until ready for extraction and then thawed and extracted in the laboratory. See WHONDRS_YDE21_Sediment_Extract_Protocol.pdf for details. Water samples and sediment extracts were shipped internationally on blue ice, but shipping time exceeded the lifespan of the ice. Upon receipt, they were refrigerated and analyzed for NPOC and FTICR-MS. For details regarding laboratory and instrument methods, see the alphanumeric methods codes located in the header rows of the chemistry data csv file and their associated definitions in YDE21_Methods_Codes.csv. Data formats follow ESS-DIVE Reporting Formats.",
      "Formularity, the software used to assign molecular formulas to peaks in FTICR-MS data, has been renamed to Formultitude, and can now be referenced via https://github.com/PNNL-Comp-Mass-Spec/Formultitude . However, the contents of this data package refer to the original name (Formularity)."
    ],
